{
  "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
  "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "SETH KRETZER",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Across Texas's 572 executions spanning four decades, the State's policy was to allow a spiritual advisor to be present in the execution chamber to lay hands on a condemned inmate and to audibly pray."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State now argues that Ramirez's resort to litigation came somehow far too late but also six days too early."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "SETH KRETZER",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "TDCJ's own history and practices, as well as the current approaches of the federal government and states like Alabama, prove that Texas's restrictions on touch and prayer are not the least restrictive means of furthering its proffered execution interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, has Mr. Ramirez always requested that hands be laid on him?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "repeated filing of complaints, particularly at the last minute, not only be seen as evidence of gaming of the system but also of the sincerity of religious beliefs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, what is your client's position on -- is it touch anywhere on his body that will satisfy his religious needs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "equal treatment principle that we enshrined in -- in Murphy or enforced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "problem close to zero. I think you're saying, ah, the risk isn't that much. But how do we analyze that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "about if another state allows bread and wine in the execution room right before the execution? Does every state have to do that because it's a less restrictive alternative?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now how do we deal with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But you can't say that, can you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0000-0017",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "over the last couple of years, we have had a whole series of stay applications that present issues that are related to the one that is presented here, and each one has been different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you haven't said anything about what you want exactly with respect to audible prayer. What type of prayer? When? How loud? What exactly do you want to start out with?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Mr. Ramirez's case, the 1983 petition was filed a month in advance of the execution date, and the district judge entered a scheduling order when the motion for stay would be filed, the response/reply. So all those proceeded very much apace, and the Fifth Circuit ruled within a few days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the State is so worried about these things coming up in the last minute, all they have to do is actually tell us what the rules are. In other words, there's not a single thing in the prison manual that anyone can see or in the form that Pastor Moore was told to sign that says what he could or could not do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you have an objection, come in and tell us what you need within a certain amount of time, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Becket Fund",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The brief the amicus of the Becket Fund filed where they showed the historical examples of where pastoral spiritual guidance has been given throughout history to people as"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But you're talking about least restrictive alternatives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: As the submissions to this Court, including today, reflect, there are continuing factual disputes on many issues that we think ultimately warrant a remand. And we'd like to think that better explaining the federal experience may be helpful for further review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, I think you're -- you've come close to answering it because I'm interested in what would be precisely in this context the State of Texas -- I know you've generically talked about it -- what would be the least restrictive means in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: May I ask more about the BOP experience? I mean, as I understand it, there were 13 recent executions. In 11, there were spiritual advisors there. You said that all of them, you allowed vocalization throughout the process, but in only one was there touching and that before the drugs were administered. Is that basically -- did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That risk may be low, but the harm, as Justice Barrett was mentioning earlier, would be extremely high. Also, unlike an --an actual prison employee, like a state or federal chaplain, the outside spiritual advisor would need to be removed if the medical team had to come in, and that in itself could cause delay or -- or problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "BOP",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: As to the chamber, Your Honor, ours has about twice the square footage of what I understand Texas's is, which is what enables us to have the spiritual advisor about nine feet away during the administration of the drugs. Before the administration of the drugs, the spiritual advisor was advised to stand at a line that's taped on the floor that's about 28 inches away from the gurney. I don't know that the precise procedures we've used there would be feasible for Texas with its smaller chamber."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I'm sorry to take up so much time. If I could just ask one more question. It relates to something that, to my mind, is related to this, although it's a different subject, and -- and that is I'm interested in BOP practice regarding religious services during a typical weekend. So, on a Friday, Saturday, Sunday, in a federal prison, what religious services, if any, are prisoners allowed to attend? Do you know the answer to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: There was someone present in 11 of the 13?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "BOP",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: And I think BOP would have a vastly greater degree of concern for the reasons I mentioned earlier about accommodating a request to have the spiritual advisor in physical contact with the inmate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: I'm just wondering if it's legitimate to define it as trying to get to zero percent risk, because, you know, Justice Alito asked you about services on the weekends. I -- I think -- it's my understanding, I might be wrong -- that BOP and -- and state prisons too do allow some religious services, perhaps because of RLUIPA. If they said, we want the risk of prison rioting or fighting to be zero percent, that would permit the prison, right, to say there can never be any kind of prayer service or gathering?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No? Certainly not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Are you aware in any other states of an execution going astray because of an outside spiritual advisor?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: I -- I would also add an important -- an important distinction, Your Honor, is that for every one of those circumstances, the individual is a TDCJ employee. And it turns out TDCJ is a correctional institution dealing with the extraordinarily charged and choreographed area of -- of a death chamber."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You have to think about the risk together with the harm, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: No, Justice Kagan, but it did indirectly in that when we had chaplains in the room, we didn't need to have another security officer in the room. And so the fact that we have a volunteer coming into the room, the chaplain has to now be -- now has to be accompanied by a security officer, which required us to take out the warden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-373ffcc23374-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 99,
        "start": 99
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I understand that prisoners --you don't have any rules that say prisoners can't pray out loud during the execution, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-5592",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "373ffcc233747286c8c020c74339d6a7c5718e5547d844a4e4e02f8924231da8",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-373ffcc23374-108",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
